---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout title="Troubleshooting & Diagnostics" currentSlug="/guide/troubleshooting">
  <div class="space-y-8 text-buddy-text">
    <div>
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-buddy-cyan font-semibold">Support</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mt-1">Troubleshooting & Diagnostics</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-buddy-muted mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Quick solutions to common issues, log inspection, and reporting glitches.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Common Issues Accordion/Cards -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Common Questions & Solutions</h2>

      <div class="space-y-3 text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-1.5">
          <b class="text-white text-sm">Where did Buddy go? I can't find him on my screen.</b>
          <p class="text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
            If Buddy wandered off to a disconnected monitor or got stuck off-screen, right-click his icon in the Windows notification tray (bottom-right near your clock) and choose <b>Bring buddy here</b>. He will immediately teleport onto your active screen.
          </p>
          <p class="text-buddy-darkMuted">
            Note: Buddy is configured by default to hide whenever a fullscreen game or video player is active, and reappears when you return to your desktop.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-1.5">
          <b class="text-white text-sm">He starts dancing when people are talking or during video games.</b>
          <p class="text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
            Open <b>Settings &rarr; Reactions &rarr; Music</b> and lower the <b>Beat lock</b> slider (e.g. to 0.35 - 0.45). This forces the rhythm detector to require several seconds of steady musical cadence before committing to a dance.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-1.5">
          <b class="text-white text-sm">Talk fails or reports an API error.</b>
          <p class="text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
            Open <b>Settings &rarr; Talk</b> and click the <b>Test</b> button. It displays the provider's exact HTTP status code and response body. Most often, the API key is expired or the provider has deprecated the selected model ID (click the ↻ refresh button next to Chat Model to fetch current models).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-buddy-bg border border-buddy-border space-y-1.5">
          <b class="text-white text-sm">Audio level meter stays completely silent while music is playing.</b>
          <p class="text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
            Ensure your default Windows audio output device is active. Some exclusive-mode ASIO or DAW sound drivers bypass the Windows WASAPI loopback mixer; switching your player to standard DirectSound/WASAPI shared mode resolves this.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Diagnostic Logs -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Diagnostic Logs</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
        When reporting a bug or unexpected behavior, attaching the diagnostic log file is immensely helpful:
      </p>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-black/50 border border-buddy-border font-mono text-xs text-buddy-cyan">
        %APPDATA%\com.rocco.robobuddy\buddy.log
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-buddy-muted">
        This file records application startups, model retargeting errors, dropped frame alerts, and WASAPI audio connection events.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- GitHub Issues Link -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-buddy-border pb-2">Still Stuck? Report an Issue</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-buddy-muted leading-relaxed">
        File an issue on our public releases tracker with your Windows version, graphics card, and the relevant lines from <code>buddy.log</code>:
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/MrSco/robo-buddy/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-buddy-card border border-buddy-border hover:border-buddy-cyan text-xs text-white font-semibold transition-colors"
      >
        <span>Open an Issue on GitHub</span>
        <span>&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation -->
    <div class="pt-6 border-t border-buddy-border flex justify-between">
      <a href="/guide/webcam-mocap" class="text-xs text-buddy-darkMuted hover:text-buddy-cyan transition-colors">&larr; Back: Webcam Mocap</a>
      <a href="/guide" class="text-xs text-buddy-cyan hover:underline">Return to Guide Index &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
